/* psx_bios_kernel_seed.c - the SCPH-1001 kernel tables in low RAM at the
 * game's first instruction, as the ROM's boot leaves them.
 *
 * Every nonzero word of the table of tables (0x100), the A0, C0 and B0
 * function tables (0x200, 0x674, 0x874), the device control blocks
 * (0x6EE0, 10 x 0x50), errno (0x8640), the file control blocks (0x8648,
 * 16 x 0x2C) and the kernel heap from 0xE000 (the exception chain at
 * 0xE004, the event table at 0xE028, the process block at 0xE294 and the
 * four thread blocks at 0xE29C, each behind its allocation header). Read
 * from a DuckStation SCPH-1001 RAM image taken at the EXE entry of Spyro 2
 * and of Spyro 3, which agree on every word here. The words of file 2 that
 * depend on the disc (the boot EXE's open) are seeded separately. Values
 * of the form 0xBFCxxxxx are ROM addresses; the code at them is not
 * modelled, and the function tables are data here, never jumped through.
 */
